WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.902
-Hi, Shepard.
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:04.336
-What's up, man?
A creative name, right?

00:00:04.336 --> 00:00:06.106
"The News." A lot of thought.
-I love --

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:09.676
-How did you get the rights
to just calling it "The News"?

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:12.745
It's genius.
-Many focus groups, man.

00:00:12.745 --> 00:00:16.015
Just, you know -- These things
come if you take time.

00:00:16.015 --> 00:00:17.784
-Welcome to the NBC family.

00:00:17.784 --> 00:00:20.753
We're excited to have you
at the network.

00:00:20.753 --> 00:00:23.989
You're at CNBC right now?
-Yep.

00:00:23.989 --> 00:00:26.659
-You are the first interview
not on Zoom

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:30.196
that I've done in six months
since we've been in quarantine,

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:31.698
so thank you for doing this.

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:33.132
This is really cool for me.

00:00:33.132 --> 00:00:34.434
-I'm happy to do it.

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:36.635
But back when
you were in quarantine

00:00:36.635 --> 00:00:39.773
and your kids
took over for The Roots,

00:00:39.773 --> 00:00:42.375
those were great shows, man.

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:44.444
I loved those
sitting at home in the box.

00:00:44.444 --> 00:00:45.912
That was a lot of fun.
-Oh, I'm happy.

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:47.380
Thank you.
Yeah, they stole the show.

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:49.081
I had to push them off
a little bit.

00:00:49.081 --> 00:00:51.184
They were getting
too big-headed.

00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:54.987
I want to ask you about a couple
things from over the weekend.

00:00:54.987 --> 00:00:59.425
Obviously "The Times" obtained
Trump's tax information.

00:00:59.425 --> 00:01:01.694
Can you tell us about that
and what is that news?

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:03.396
Explain the big takeaway there.

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:06.332
-We haven't confirmed it at
CNBC, but from the reporting,

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:07.967
I feel like
what stuck out for me was

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:10.669
he spent 70 grand on hair
for television.

00:01:10.669 --> 00:01:14.407
I'm not sure
that there was great value.

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:18.511
But, seriously, you know,
11 of the last 18 years,

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:19.979
according to
"The Times'" reporting,

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:22.515
he didn't -- he avoided
paying taxes at all.

00:01:22.515 --> 00:01:24.083
-Yeah.

00:01:24.083 --> 00:01:27.453
-He had a lot more dealings
with special-interest groups

00:01:27.453 --> 00:01:29.422
in the United States
and overseas

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:31.958
than we knew
before this reporting,

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:35.027
though there's nothing new
on any Russian parts of it all.

00:01:35.027 --> 00:01:39.499
We know that Ivanka was
receiving some consulting money

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:41.800
that cut down on his taxes.

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:45.338
And, you know, there was a lot
of that sort of thing.

00:01:45.338 --> 00:01:46.605
What does it all add up to?

00:01:46.605 --> 00:01:49.608
I'm not sure it'll matter
to his faithful.

00:01:49.608 --> 00:01:51.777
The Never Trumpers
are still Never Trumpers.

00:01:51.777 --> 00:01:54.546
And whether the people in
the middle pay attention to that

00:01:54.546 --> 00:01:56.048
or not, I don't know.

00:01:56.048 --> 00:01:58.585
But "The Times" says there's
more investigating coming

00:01:58.585 --> 00:02:00.553
and more reports,
so we'll watch for it.

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:01.988
-Yeah.

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:04.357
Well, obviously the sad news

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:06.759
that Ruth Bader Ginsburg
passed away.

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:09.329
And over the weekend,
Trump nominated conservative

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:12.931
Amy Coney Barrett
to the Supreme Court.

00:02:12.931 --> 00:02:14.867
And he says that he wants her
to be confirmed

00:02:14.867 --> 00:02:16.369
before the election.

00:02:16.369 --> 00:02:18.070
Do you think
that's going to happen?

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:20.239
-It could.
They say it's going to happen,

00:02:20.239 --> 00:02:22.708
that they can make it happen
in that amount of time.

00:02:22.708 --> 00:02:24.510
She's the darling
of conservatives.

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:28.214
The evangelical crew loves her.

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:30.416
He wants -- He's been talking
from the very beginning

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:33.285
about how judges
will be his legacy.

00:02:33.285 --> 00:02:35.821
And whether it'll affect
the election or not,

00:02:35.821 --> 00:02:37.223
it probably will.

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:38.958
You just don't know which way
it's going to play, Jimmy.

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:41.727
You know, will conservatives
be so happy about it

00:02:41.727 --> 00:02:44.163
that they come out
and vote for more

00:02:44.163 --> 00:02:46.065
or will Democrats
and people on the left say,

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:47.533
"We can't let this
happen again,"

00:02:47.533 --> 00:02:49.235
and come out and vote
in bigger numbers?

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:50.903
I don't think we'll know
till we know.

00:02:50.903 --> 00:02:56.108
-Yeah. Trump is now
questioning the election --

00:02:56.108 --> 00:02:59.412
the validity of the election
should he lose.

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:02.248
-Well, of this, I'm certain.

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:04.016
There is nothing to indicate

00:03:04.016 --> 00:03:06.552
that there's
widespread voter fraud

00:03:06.552 --> 00:03:09.555
on a local level
or on the national level.

00:03:09.555 --> 00:03:12.292
That's reportable,
and that's factual.

00:03:12.292 --> 00:03:14.761
The rest of it,
I'm not exactly sure

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:16.863
what it is
he's trying to accomplish.

00:03:16.863 --> 00:03:18.898
Because there is
no evidence of that.

00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:20.833
I'm sure that
there's some thinking

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:23.469
that if it doesn't go well maybe
he'll be able to point to that.

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:25.938
He made these same sorts
of accusations

00:03:25.938 --> 00:03:29.075
before the last election
regarding Hillary Clinton.

00:03:29.075 --> 00:03:32.111
So sometimes you have to
just watch what's happening

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:34.613
and listen to what they're
saying just a little bit less.

00:03:34.613 --> 00:03:37.083
Not just the President,
but most of them, Jimmy.

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:39.452
-Yeah. Maybe he's just trying
to hype up his base and be like,

00:03:39.452 --> 00:03:41.721
"Yeah, it's going to be rigged,
so you better get out there

00:03:41.721 --> 00:03:43.389
and vote because
it's going to be rigged,

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:45.023
and if we just win
by a landslide,

00:03:45.023 --> 00:03:47.560
then we won't have to have
this conversation."

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:52.364
-And, also, "If I don't win,
here might be the reason."

00:03:52.364 --> 00:03:54.099
He's managed expectations
in this way

00:03:54.099 --> 00:03:55.668
throughout his business career.

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:57.837
You wonder if maybe he's
taking a page from that now.

00:03:57.837 --> 00:03:59.105
I don't know.

00:03:59.105 --> 00:04:01.040
-The first presidential debate
is tomorrow night.

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:02.808
It is going to be moderated
by your former

00:04:02.808 --> 00:04:04.877
Fox News colleague
Chris Wallace.

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:07.446
What do you expect to see
in the debate tomorrow night?

00:04:07.446 --> 00:04:08.947
What should we expect?

00:04:08.947 --> 00:04:12.218
-I expect Chris Wallace
to be prepared.

00:04:12.218 --> 00:04:14.220
Nobody who has watched
Chris Wallace

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:16.856
thinks other than
that he's a very tough,

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:19.959
very thoroughly prepared
journalist.

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:22.027
And he's said repeatedly
over the years,

00:04:22.027 --> 00:04:23.829
to me and publicly,

00:04:23.829 --> 00:04:25.698
"My job is to
stay out of the way

00:04:25.698 --> 00:04:28.434
and be unnoticed
as much as possible."

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:33.005
But he's not one to let a
falsehood or a misrepresentation

00:04:33.005 --> 00:04:35.440
or a "look over here"
kind of shiny object thing

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:37.343
just slide by the way.

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:39.946
He will hold them.
Both of them.

00:04:39.946 --> 00:04:43.283
He's not a partisan guy.
He's searching for truth.

00:04:43.283 --> 00:04:45.084
He's trying
to speak truth to power

00:04:45.084 --> 00:04:47.219
and trying to get information
to the public.

00:04:47.219 --> 00:04:49.054
That's what all journalists
want to do.

00:04:49.054 --> 00:04:50.590
It's not about Chris.

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:52.024
He'll be the first
to tell you that.

00:04:52.024 --> 00:04:56.662
It's about finding out
what they are really about.

00:04:56.662 --> 00:04:59.698
-That's a good segue
into your new show.

00:04:59.698 --> 00:05:01.934
You certainly couldn't have
picked a more critical time

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:05.438
in our nation's history
to start your new show.

00:05:05.438 --> 00:05:06.839
There's so much news to cover.

00:05:06.839 --> 00:05:10.476
Tell us about "The News
with Shepard Smith."

00:05:10.476 --> 00:05:12.578
-It'll be that simple.
It'll be the news.

00:05:12.578 --> 00:05:15.548
We're not going to have pundits.
We're not going to have opinion.

00:05:15.548 --> 00:05:18.984
We'll bring you facts.
The facts, the truth, the news.

00:05:18.984 --> 00:05:22.354
We'll try to bring it to you
in context and with perspective.

00:05:22.354 --> 00:05:25.324
When we see things that are not
true, like that shiny object

00:05:25.324 --> 00:05:28.127
I was talking about,
we'll point that out.

00:05:28.127 --> 00:05:30.262
And we'll cut through
the disinformation.

00:05:30.262 --> 00:05:33.166
Jimmy, there's so much of it.
It's all over our feeds.

00:05:33.166 --> 00:05:37.536
Sometimes people live
in a world of just lies.

00:05:37.536 --> 00:05:39.138
And when that's happening

00:05:39.138 --> 00:05:42.107
and it rises to the public
discourse, we'll point it out.

00:05:42.107 --> 00:05:44.443
Look, there was a time
when all newscasts

00:05:44.443 --> 00:05:46.078
or most of them were just,

00:05:46.078 --> 00:05:48.948
"Here are the facts,
so you can decide for yourself.

00:05:48.948 --> 00:05:50.549
Here's what's happening
in the world

00:05:50.549 --> 00:05:52.217
so you can plan
for your family

00:05:52.217 --> 00:05:54.920
and your business and
your community and your church."

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:56.322
That's what we want to do.

00:05:56.322 --> 00:06:00.292
We want to be a source
of truth and honesty,

00:06:00.292 --> 00:06:02.761
and we'll hold truth to power
because that is our job.

00:06:02.761 --> 00:06:05.197
The founding fathers
didn't only put journalism

00:06:05.197 --> 00:06:06.932
in the Constitution
for no reason.

00:06:06.932 --> 00:06:08.701
They put it there
because it's important,

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:11.036
and journalists have
a responsibility to get it right

00:06:11.036 --> 00:06:13.539
and tell it straight, and
that's what we're going to do.

00:06:13.539 --> 00:06:17.576
-It premiers this Wednesday
at 7:00 p.m.

00:06:17.576 --> 00:06:19.145
You're going to be on
every night.

00:06:19.145 --> 00:06:21.280
Congrats on this and good luck
with the new show.

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:22.748
I'll be watching.

00:06:22.748 --> 00:06:24.549
-Thank you, Jimmy.
Really appreciate it.

00:06:24.549 --> 00:06:26.952
-Thanks again for coming
on the show. Stay safe, please.

00:06:26.952 --> 00:06:30.022
Shepard Smith, everybody.
"The News with Shepard Smith"

00:06:30.022 --> 00:06:33.826
premiers this Wednesday
at 7:00 p.m. on CNBC.

00:06:33.826 --> 00:06:35.895
Set your DVRs.

